Title: The Misfortune of Meaning
Credit: Written by Lee Brandt
Draft date: September 2025

FADE IN:

### ACT I – THE FRONT

INT. CHARLES’ APARTMENT – NIGHT

CHARLES HONEYCUTT, 40s, balding and meek, types away on his detective novel in a stained bathrobe.

        CHARLES (V.O.)
    They say every man has a story. Mine just never seemed to sell.

INT. PAGE TURNERS PUBLISHING – DAY

Stacks of books. A fake publishing house. QUEENIE TURNER runs the fencing op.

        QUEENIE
    Ship ten cases to the Goldstein drop. Mark 'em as bulk orders from a university.

EDDIE, her little brother, is tinkering with a hacked POS system in the back.

REECEY, the youngest Turner, talks down a courier with psych-major precision.

INT. TURNER HOUSE – NIGHT

Enter ROBBIE DUPREE, 18. Big, dopey, sincere. He lifts a refrigerator solo. Queenie pays him cash.

        REECEY
    You didn’t *have* to carry it inside.

        ROBBIE
    Wanted to. Also... hi.

REECEY smiles politely. Nothing more.

### ACT II – THE SPARK

INT. ART GALLERY – NIGHT

Eccentric elite reads a line from Charles’ latest novel.

        SNOBBY WOMAN
    “The shadows stretched long... like the disappointment in his father's voice.”

Nods of pretentious approval.

INT. PAGE TURNERS HQ – NIGHT

Queenie watches a BookTuber review Charles’ book.

        YOUTUBER (ON SCREEN)
    It’s like Bukowski ghostwrote for Black Mirror and gave up halfway through. Five stars.

INT. CHARLES’ APARTMENT – NIGHT

Charles opens a royalty check. Smiles. Has no idea it's cartel money.

INT. FEDERAL TASK FORCE OFFICE – DAY

LT. HARPER pins photos to a corkboard. Charles. Queenie. Eddie. Red string everywhere.

INT. BACK ALLEY – NIGHT

KEVIN HART GUY rants at Queenie and Eddie. Wants a bigger cut. Robbie just stands behind Queenie, cracking his knuckles.

        KEVIN HART GUY
    I’m the reason your scam works! I *am* the brand!

        QUEENIE
    Robbie, look tired yet?

        ROBBIE
    Not yet.

Kevin Hart Guy walks off.

### ACT III – THE INFERNO

INT. PAGE TURNERS HQ – NIGHT

Reecey confronts Queenie.

        REECEY
    This isn’t small-time anymore. You said we were getting out.

        QUEENIE
    We are. After one more.

INT. SAFEHOUSE STAGING – DAY

Queenie plans the gala job. One last hit. Everyone’s nervous. Even Robbie looks unsure.

INT. PARKING LOT – NIGHT

Harper interviews a gallery staffer. Conspiracy theorist livestreams nearby.

INT. BODEGA – DAY

Cartel goon eyes a photo of Kevin Hart Guy on his burner.

        CARTEL GOON
    That’s him. That’s the punk with my daughter.

### ACT IV – THE GALA

INT. BALLROOM – NIGHT

Charles is in a wrinkled suit. Holding his latest manuscript: _The Honeycutt Affair_.

        CHARLES
    ...and that’s when the bullet hit the statue—

**BANG.** Kevin Hart Guy drops.

Screams. Harper draws. Cartel goon flees.

Robbie steps in front of Reecey as chaos erupts—and is shot protecting her.

        REECEY (screaming)
    Robbie!!

Charles claps once, thinking it's a performance piece.

INT. BACK HALL – MOMENTS LATER

Queenie grabs Eddie. Reecey is shaking. Cops swarm in.

        HARPER
    Everyone down! Now!

### ACT V – THE DEAL

INT. INTERROGATION ROOM – DAY

Queenie lays it all out for the feds.

        QUEENIE
    We weren’t saints. But we weren’t the devil either. We stole from Wal-Mart with murder contracts.

INT. FEDERAL SAFEHOUSE – MONTAGE

New names. Witness protection.

- Eddie works at a garage.
- Reecey starts school again.
- Queenie waters plants in a quiet home.

### ACT VI – THE REWRITE

INT. BOOKSTORE – DAY

Charles signs copies of _The Honeycutt Affair_.

        FAN
    Is it based on a true story?

        CHARLES
    Writers write what they know.

INT. SUBURBAN LIVING ROOM – NIGHT

KEVIN HART GUY is alive. Tucks kids into bed. Watches Charles on TV.

        KEVIN
    Desk job for now. Missed bedtime.

FADE OUT.